TCLAP - Templatized Command Line Argument Parser

This is a simple C++ library that facilitates parsing command line
arguments in a type independent manner. It doesn't conform exactly
to either the GNU or POSIX standards, although it is close. See
docs/manual.html for descriptions of how things work or look at the
simple examples in the examples dir.

Recommended versions
--------------------

  1.2  For existing integrations that require the legacy 1.2 API or
       behavior. Receives only critical bug fixes.
  1.4  Recommended for projects requiring C++98 compatibility.
       Maintenance version with no new feature development.
  1.6  Recommended for projects using C++20 or later. Modernized
       internals with an API mostly source compatible with 1.4.

Choose the version that matches your project's C++ and API requirements.

The optional CMake build requires CMake 3.13 or later.

Any and all feedback is welcome at https://sf.net/p/tclap/discussion/
